;;; The blind rung never proposes an arity-3 fact, and the run was certified
;;; anyway — **W6**'s second witness. Register row
;;; `W6/arity3` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`).
;;;
;;; The goal is `(r3 ?x ?y ?z)`. `hypgen`'s `fill_slot` documents that arity ≥ 3
;;; is unenumerated, so the rung proposes the two `r2` facts it can build and
;;; nothing over `r3`. The engine answered
;;;
;;;   Solution k = 1, `{(r2 A B), (r2 B A)}`, `exhausted = true`
;;;
;;; — certified, over a goal relation no commitment ever touched.
;;;
;;; The right answer is Q-M1e2.3's: R is over the universe as the blind rung
;;; builds it (arity 3 unenumerated), so `exhausted = true` is true of R, and
;;; the read-out names what the universe leaves out, here the goal relation
;;; `r3`.
;;;
;;; `ein solve` answers R, four states over the two `r2` candidates,
;;; exhausted, and every question names what the universe leaves out, under
;;; `universe`:
;;;
;;;   outside   r3 — no candidate: it has arity 3, and the blind enumerator
;;;             proposes arity 1 and 2 only. R holds of it only what the
;;;             program states and saturation derives
;;;
;;; `is-a` is not named: the program scopes it out itself. The register's
;;; row is fixed.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;;
(relation is-a T T :why "{?1} is a {?2}")
(relation r3 T T T :why "r3 holds of {?1}, {?2} and {?3}")
(relation r2 T T :why "r2 holds of {?1} and {?2}")
(is-a A T) (is-a B T)
(solve :no-hypothesis (is-a))
(query :goal (r3 ?x ?y ?z))
